WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.717
Priya moves her group to a new insurer on July 1.

00:00:03.717 --> 00:00:07.771
Without protection, her employees would face a second deductible in one year.

00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:11.826
A deductible carryover, or transfer of credit, provision counts expenses applied to

00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:15.880
the old plan’s deductible toward the new plan’s deductible for the rest

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.935
of the year, and the same for coinsurance toward the out-of-pocket maximum.

00:00:19.935 --> 00:00:24.665
The no-loss no-gain rule requires the new carrier to cover employees as the old

00:00:24.665 --> 00:00:29.395
plan would have, including those currently disabled or hospitalized, so no one loses coverage

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:33.450
because of the change and no one gains benefits they lacked before.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:38.914
An employee’s coverage terminates when employment ends or hours fall below the eligible

00:00:38.914 --> 00:00:44.379
class, when the employee stops paying a required contribution, when the employer terminates

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:49.002
the master policy, or when the employee enters the armed forces.

00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:53.626
A dependent’s coverage ends when the dependent no longer qualifies, for

00:00:53.626 --> 00:00:57.830
example a child turning 26 or a spouse after divorce.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:02.033
Each termination triggers rights: continuation, conversion or special enrollment elsewhere.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:06.657
Maryland requires the certificate to explain these rights, and employers must

00:01:06.657 --> 00:01:10.860
give notice promptly so that election deadlines can be met.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.861
An employee called to active duty may continue group coverage for

00:01:14.861 --> 00:01:18.862
up to 24 months under federal law and, on return, must

00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:22.864
be reinstated in the plan without a new waiting period or

00:01:22.864 --> 00:01:26.865
exclusion for conditions other than service-connected injuries, which the military covers.

00:01:26.865 --> 00:01:31.594
Group certificates also carry notices about Medicare eligibility, because turning 65 changes how

00:01:31.594 --> 00:01:36.322
the plan coordinates: for employers with 20 or more employees the group plan

00:01:36.322 --> 00:01:41.051
remains primary for active workers, and the employee should weigh Part B enrollment.

00:01:41.051 --> 00:01:44.689
Extension of benefits continues coverage for a totally disabled employee’s

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:48.326
existing condition for a period after the master policy terminates,

00:01:48.326 --> 00:01:51.600
so a canceled policy does not abandon someone mid-treatment.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.270
Federal COBRA applies to employers with 20 or more employees.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:01.873
Termination for reasons other than gross misconduct, or reduced hours, allows 18

00:02:01.873 --> 00:02:07.477
months of continuation; disability extends it to 29 months; death, divorce, Medicare

00:02:07.477 --> 00:02:12.146
entitlement or a child aging out gives dependents 36 months.

00:02:12.146 --> 00:02:17.283
The employer notifies the plan within 30 days, the plan notifies

00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:22.419
the beneficiary within 14 days, the beneficiary elects within 60 days

00:02:22.419 --> 00:02:27.089
and pays the first premium within 45 days of electing.

00:02:27.089 --> 00:02:32.693
The premium may be up to 102 percent of the full cost.

00:02:32.693 --> 00:02:39.230
Coverage ends early for nonpayment, new group coverage or the employer dropping all plans.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:42.516
Maryland’s own continuation statutes reach group contracts of

00:02:42.516 --> 00:02:45.802
any size, including those too small for COBRA.

00:02:45.802 --> 00:02:50.321
After a loss of employment for reasons other than cause, an

00:02:50.321 --> 00:02:54.839
insured covered for at least three months may continue for up

00:02:54.839 --> 00:02:59.358
to 18 months, electing within 45 days, at no more than

00:02:59.358 --> 00:03:03.877
the combined employer and employee contribution plus an approved administrative fee.

00:03:03.877 --> 00:03:08.806
After the insured’s death, a spouse covered at least 30 days and

00:03:08.806 --> 00:03:13.324
dependent children may continue for 18 months on the same terms.

00:03:13.324 --> 00:03:17.432
After divorce, a former spouse covered 30 days may continue

00:03:17.432 --> 00:03:21.540
until remarriage or other coverage, with the insured paying through

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.237
payroll deduction unless a court or agreement provides otherwise.

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:26.880
Medicare entitlement ends continuation.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.430
Continuation keeps the group plan for a time;

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.535
conversion replaces it with an individual policy.

00:03:33.535 --> 00:03:39.303
Under a conversion privilege, a person whose group coverage ends may buy an

00:03:39.303 --> 00:03:45.071
individual policy from the same insurer within 31 days without evidence of insurability.

00:03:45.071 --> 00:03:49.952
The individual policy may have different benefits and a higher premium.

00:03:49.952 --> 00:03:52.614
Maryland’s continuation statutes preserve conversion rights.

00:03:52.614 --> 00:03:57.938
Since the Affordable Care Act made individual coverage guaranteed issue, conversion matters

00:03:57.938 --> 00:04:03.263
less for medical plans, but an employee leaving Priya’s bakery still has

00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:08.587
three doors: Maryland continuation or COBRA, conversion with the carrier, or a

00:04:08.587 --> 00:04:12.580
special enrollment on Maryland Health Connection within 60 days.
